Therefore, the perimeter of triangle $AMN$ is simply \begin{align*}
AM + AN + MN &= AM + AN + MI + NI \\
&= AM + AN + MB + NC \\
&= (AM + MB) + (AN + NC) \\
&= AB + AC \\
&= 17 + 24 \\
&= \boxed{41}.
\end{align*}

Because $\triangle PQR$ is isosceles with $PQ=QR$, median $\overline{QM}$ is also an altitude:


